\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
with a key-version prefix. It is stateless, so a manifest committed days earlier still verifies, and a token copied from someone else's repo fails because the binding differs. It is public by design, so its value is binding, not secrecy. G2 proves one att
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 ributable party controls both source and origin. It does not prove the deployed bytes were built from that source.
